   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Trooper Lawrence P. Gleason Memorial Bridge\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S2904",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2904-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-o, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2904\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Trooper Lawrence P. Gleason Memorial\nBridge\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo name a state bridge in the town of Schroon in honor of Trooper\nLawrence P. Gleason, who was killed in 2002 in the line of duty.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Designates the overpass on Charley Hill Road, over Inter-\nstate 87, in the town of Schroon the \"Trooper Lawrence P.  Gleason Memo-\nrial Bridge\".\n\nSection 2 - Directs the commissioner of Transportation to provide and\nmaintain signage\n\nSection 3 - Provides effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOn Feb. 11, 2002, 28-year-old Trooper Lawrence P. Gleason was killed by\nan armed man while responding to a domestic violence complaint in Crown\nPoint.\n\nA member of Troop B, Trooper Gleason was stationed in Schroon Lake.\nTrooper Gleason's sacrifice and valor are remembered and honored to this\nday throughout Essex County. It is only right that his sacrifice be\nhonored by the state.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022/2021: S9320 referred to Transportation; A10589 referred to Trans-\nportation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
